-- #1443 control: main.mdk with the ONE variable changed -- the unbound name is
-- replaced by a bound one. Must check clean at exit 0, which is what proves the
-- unbound name is genuinely the only reason main.mdk does not typecheck, i.e.
-- that the MCP tool's `"ok":true` really is a green on a NON-typechecking file.
main = println 1
